## MCO / HEALTH PLAN CONTRACTS — WIN FACTORS

**MCO contracts have different dynamics than government RFPs. Adjust win strategy accordingly.**

### MCO Win Position Scorecard

| Factor | Status | Score | Gap | Action to Close |
|--------|--------|-------|-----|-----------------|
| **Warm Introduction** | [Referred/Cold] | [0-10] | | Get intro from existing partner, broker, or industry contact |
| **Problem-Solution Fit** | [Exact/Close/Weak] | [0-10] | | Identify their specific pain point (cost, compliance, coverage gaps) |
| **Proof of Scale** | [Demonstrated/Claimed/None] | [0-10] | | Show volume capacity (trips/month, members served, geography) |
| **Existing Relationship** | [Active/Prior/None] | [0-10] | | Leverage any existing DDI touchpoint with the MCO |
| **Compliance Ready** | [All/Most/Some] | [0-10] | | HIPAA, BAA, state Medicaid requirements, credentialing |
| **Pricing Competitive** | [Below/Market/Above] | [0-10] | | Know their current costs, price to save them money |
| **Champion Inside** | [Yes/Building/No] | [0-10] | | Identify internal advocate who wants DDI to win |
| **TOTAL** | | **/70** | | |

### MCO Sales Cycle — Different from RFPs

| Government RFP | MCO Contract |
|----------------|--------------|
| Formal solicitation with deadline | Often informal — relationship-driven |
| Evaluation committee scores | Single decision-maker or small team |
| Public process, limited contact | Private — can build relationship throughout |
| Price often weighted heavily | Value + relationship often matter more |
| Win on paper | Win through meetings + demonstrations |

### MCO Win Actions

**Gap: No Warm Introduction**
- Find mutual connection (LinkedIn, industry events, broker network)
- Ask existing partners for referrals (Uber Health, Quest, lab partners)
- Attend MCO-specific conferences (AHIP, state Medicaid events)

**Gap: No Champion Inside**
- Identify the person with the problem DDI solves (NEMT director, pharmacy ops, member services)
- Provide value before asking for contract (data, insights, pilot offer)
- Make them look good to their leadership

**Gap: Pricing Unknown**
- Research their current vendor contracts (public filings, news, industry intel)
- Understand their PMPM structure and margins
- Offer pilot/proof-of-concept at reduced risk

**Gap: Compliance Not Ready**
- Get BAA signed early (shows seriousness)
- Complete credentialing proactively
- Have insurance/bonding ready to present

### MCO Pursuit Checklist

Before pursuing any MCO contract:
- [ ] Identified specific problem DDI solves for this MCO
- [ ] Have or can get warm introduction
- [ ] Know their current vendor and pain points
- [ ] Compliance docs ready (BAA, insurance, credentials)
- [ ] Pricing strategy that saves them money or adds value
- [ ] Clear next step (meeting, pilot, RFI response)

